From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Redpanda Data <hi@redpanda.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Make configure.ac detectable by autoconf >= 2.72

autoconf 2.72 changed autoreconf's detection of autoconf scripts: it now
greps configure.ac for a literal `AC_INIT` token (after stripping `#` and
`dnl` comments) and bails out with

    autoreconf: error: configure.ac: AC_INIT not found; not an autoconf script?

when none is found. krb5's configure.ac only calls the custom K5_AC_INIT
macro (which itself expands to AC_INIT), so the token never appears
literally and autoreconf >= 2.72 refuses to run, breaking the krb5 build
on hosts with newer autoconf (e.g. autoconf 2.73).

Add an m4_define whose body mentions AC_INIT. This is a definition, not a
call, so it does not double-initialize the package, but it makes the
literal AC_INIT token appear on a non-comment line so autoreconf's grep
succeeds. autoconf/autoheader then run normally and produce configure as
before.
---
 src/configure.ac | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/configure.ac b/src/configure.ac
--- a/src/configure.ac
+++ b/src/configure.ac
@@ -1,4 +1,5 @@
 K5_AC_INIT([aclocal.m4])
+m4_define([_k5_ac_init_present],[AC_INIT])
 
 # If $runstatedir isn't set by autoconf (<2.70), set it manually.
 if test x"$runstatedir" = x; then
